# Check every text file out with LF on every platform.
#
# Several guard tests read this repository's own files and assert on exact
# lines — the C6 brand guard's README heading, and the release-hardening
# suite's `\n`-anchored workflow regexes. Under Git's default `core.autocrlf`
# on Windows those files arrive CRLF, so the assertions compare against bytes
# CI never sees and fail for a reason that has nothing to do with the code.
#
# Nothing here needs CRLF; `.sh` and the Dockerfiles positively require LF.
* text=auto eol=lf
